      "writtenOn": "2022-12-23T04:52:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because that code continues with\n\n    setProbesStatus(probesSucceeded, probesSucceeded);\n\nObserve how that bitmask is passed to both `probesCompleted` and `probesSucceeded`. So if this value is true in `setNetworkValid()`, then the probe is considered to have been sent and to have succeeded. That makes sense because it\u0027s `setNetworkValid()`, so of course the probe has succeeded.\n\nConversely in `setNetworkInvalid`, it decides whether the probe has been sent. Because that method never declares the private DNS probes to have succeeded, it ends up meaning the probe has been sent but failed. `setNetworkInvalid` has no way to say that the private DNS probe has been sent, succeeded, but something else failed afterwards. The reason we don\u0027t have a way to say that is because it was never necessary so far. This patch is only a rename and should not change that existing behavior ; in fact, if we ever need to add a way to tell that the network is invalid but for some other reason, this rename will make it much easier to understand.",
